Modification: the harness's second look now writes every entry the way the memory writes its own names, and the harness itself checks that it changed nothing else. `solver/passes.py` gains a completion bullet for an entry the key does not carry -- the list writes an entry's complete name and nothing else, no listed string is a shortened form and none carries a title the list never uses, so a name the answer wrote short is written out in full and a title the answer appended is left off, the same entry and not another -- and a guard that reads the entries out of both `final_answer` fields (split on the separator the memory itself joins its answers with, the problem's markup taken off first) and discards the check's answer unless the two read as the answer's own entries: the same number of them, each one the check's own version of the entry the answer chose, none added, none dropped, none exchanged for a different entry (`same_entry`: the rewrite's letters hold the answer's in order, or the two are prefix-related, which is a name written out or a title dropped and nothing else). `solver/tools/retrieval.py` exposes `memory_joiner()` and `solver/agent.py` gates the completion bullet on it: a memory whose answers are single strings, which is USPTO's 0/50 and Symptom2Disease's 0/200 joined answers, has no name to write out in full, so those two tasks keep the parent's conservative bullet and only a memory that joins several entries per answer gets the completion licence. No extra model call is added; no dataset name, label list or keyword list is used and no Val or Test label is fed back.

